			<tr>
				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">Unkempt Preservers (Druids)</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2690">Bickelhaupt</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/27/2002 - 7:00 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2143">Bickelhaupt</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2578">Scandyl</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														A few of us were killing time and Cyclopes in RM last night and a debate started about the relative values/penalties of hunting the Unkept preservers.<br />
<br />
The only real faction hit seems to be with &quot;QRG protected animals&quot; http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?faction=123<br />
<br />
 This looks like a port into Surefall glade might get risky						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3707">Capias</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/27/2002 - 2:28 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2989">Capias Maximus</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Yeah, looks like we probably made the right call not hunting the preservers.  Evidently the bears behind the waterfall in Surefall have their own faction (weird), and if they aggro you, then the otherwise-friendly NPC Rangers nearby will come and help kill you fast.  <br />
<br />
Probably not a big deal for most, but as a Ranger who sometimes uses the trainers there I'd hate to screw up that faction too much.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3111">ktadema</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/28/2002 - 4:20 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2488">Givins Ntakhiens</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2861">Felious Gudlious</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2487">Izzek Krakumheads</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Hey, I just hated the thought of killing something that conned amiably!  And plus they were cute lil halflings.  How can anyone kill those??<br />
Oh well, good thing we didn't I guess.						</td>
					</tr>
